  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Given that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} & -10 \\\\ -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} & \u2217 \\\\ -5 & 8 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${b}_{33}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot 8-(-5)\\cdot (-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =48-5{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}48-5{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ 45-5{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 9-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (3-x)(3+x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-3$ and $x=3.$",
